+# Plugin export and MCP ownership boundaries
+
+The existing plugin adapter owns package discovery and export. The installation record and
+per-plugin grants keep their existing owners. This change adds no store, grant, dependency or
+migration; it corrects two reproduced crossings of those boundaries.
+
+## Export
+
+`exportAgentPluginsPackage` produces a portable package without carrying configuration credentials.
+It reads only package files, never resolved user configuration or environment values. Standard
+`mcp.json` / `.mcp.json`, inline declarations and manifest-referenced MCP files share the same
+discovery and sanitization rules. Referenced files are rewritten with sanitized declarations;
+their other fields, executable files, Skills and ordinary assets remain available.
+
+- Omit server `headers`, `auth` and `oauth`, reporting every omission.
+- Preserve environment placeholders; replace literal MCP environment values with same-name
+  placeholders and report that the recipient must supply them. Field names cannot prove that an
+  arbitrary literal is not a credential. Preserve non-sensitive `userConfig` defaults and remove
+  defaults explicitly marked sensitive.
+- Import the existing `fleet.workbench` extension's `userConfig` into the ordinary manifest view;
+  explicit root-format fields keep priority. Sensitive values omitted by export remain missing
+  until the recipient configures them through the existing options owner.
+- Omit local `.env` and its variants with an explicit skipped-file reason. Preserve parseable
+  `.env.example`, `.env.sample` and `.env.template` as templates with variable placeholders; omit
+  unparseable templates with a reason. Only pure variable expressions may remain verbatim in env
+  values; mixed literal-and-variable credentials are replaced too. Do not claim to scan arbitrary
+  executable code or document prose for secrets.
+- Reject unreadable/malformed declared MCP sources before writing a destination. Never follow a
+  package symlink to copy outside content or overwrite an existing destination. Failure must not
+  leave a partially copied package containing raw credentials.
+
+```text
+package sources → existing MCP parser → sanitized export plan → copy safe assets / write configs
+```
+
+Acceptance uses synthetic credentials in inline, root and custom-path configurations, literal env
+and sensitive defaults. Verify the whole exported tree has no marker, ordinary fields/scripts/Skills
+survive, placeholders remain, and source bytes do not change. Test malformed-source failure and
+symlinks without reading a real profile.
+
+## MCP ownership
+
+The public MCP name stays `plugin:<plugin-name>:<server-key>` for compatibility with existing tool
+names, permissions, official integrations and Skills. Discovery compares the full `name@marketplace`
+owners before publishing runnable servers. Different owners claiming the same public MCP name
+cause an explicit diagnostic and remove that name from every claimant's runnable metadata and the
+combined runtime configuration. Other servers and package content remain available.
+
+A view resolves its server from its own plugin's current runnable metadata before using the shared
+MCP port. A previously connected name cannot bypass a current collision, disable or grant failure.
+Removing the conflict restores the original name. No ambiguous alias is redirected to another
+plugin; no permission rule is renamed or migrated. A connection is refreshed from the currently
+owned configuration so an older connected process cannot receive another package's calls.
+The existing MCP port carries an optional Host-only expected configuration to the pool/adapter's
+last dispatch check, including connection/recovery awaits. It is never sent over UI or MCP wire
+formats. If a shared lease changed owners while a view was connecting, the old request refuses
+instead of reaching the replacement. Calls without this option keep their behavior. An operation
+already dispatched returns its own result; changing availability never cancels and replays it.
+Equality uses the connection pool's existing canonical configuration representation, so omitted
+optional fields and explicit `undefined` remain equivalent.
+The canonical identity is frozen on the existing connection record, not recomputed from the
+caller's mutable configuration object after connection.
+
+```text
+discover packages → full-owner collision check → publish runnable names → view validates owner
+                                                                    → connect current config → call
+```
+
+Acceptance installs two real local-market packages with the same plugin name and MCP key. Verify
+both calls refuse without writing either data directory, including A connected before B is enabled.
+Disable/remove the conflict and verify each remaining owner can recover under its original name.
+Distinct server keys coexist and modify only their owning package's data. Existing official server
+names and ordinary one-plugin flows remain unchanged. Resident Agent MCP/Skill withdrawal remains
+the separately recorded lifecycle gap; this correction covers discovery and the view dispatch path.
+
+## Source basis
+
+ZCode `29628c9` supplies the existing namespace, discovery and MCP connection ownership. Agent
+Plugins 1.0.0 / HarnessRouter `protocol/versions/2026-09-28/plugins.md` supplies the portable package
+and credential-omission contract. Its latest inspected HEAD `822550ea8847d056ca789a2bb6977890a4276c5c`
+has the same contract bytes as retained latest-source `6e05aef5dc2bb25faf202130398e1509a880e166`.
+No reference checkout or pin is changed.
